{
  "info": {
    "name": "SwarmPay · be the agent",
    "description": "Play the agent against SwarmPay's agent interface (MCP over HTTP) and see the payment boundary hold.\n\n**Against the live site or any SwarmPay:** sign in, open **Agents** in the workspace header, create an agent token, and copy it and a plan ID into the environment as `agentToken` and `workflowId`. Run **2 · Be the agent** only. Approve the plan and authorize catering in the SwarmPay UI first; the agent's early request for the catering payment is then held by AgentSafe.\n\n**Against a local simulated demo** (`docker compose up`, see the README): run the whole collection with the *SwarmPay local* environment. **1 · Organizer setup** plays the human, from sign-in to an authorized catering payment, and issues the agent token; **3 · Clean up** revokes it.\n\nThe agent's token acts for its organizer only and can never approve a plan; every payment it asks for goes through AgentSafe.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// MCP over HTTP: keep the session the server issued, and start a new one on initialize.",
          "if (pm.request.url.getPath().endsWith('/mcp') && pm.request.body && pm.request.body.raw) {",
          "  const message = JSON.parse(pm.variables.replaceIn(pm.request.body.raw));",
          "  if (message.method === 'initialize') { pm.collectionVariables.unset('mcpSession'); }",
          "  else if (pm.collectionVariables.get('mcpSession')) {",
          "    pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Mcp-Session-Id', value: pm.collectionVariables.get('mcpSession') });",
          "    pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'MCP-Protocol-Version', value: pm.collectionVariables.get('mcpProtocol') || '2025-11-25' });",
          "  }",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Read an MCP reply whether it came as JSON or as a server-sent event stream.",
          "if (pm.request.url.getPath().endsWith('/mcp') && pm.response.code === 200) {",
          "  const session = pm.response.headers.get('Mcp-Session-Id');",
          "  if (session) { pm.collectionVariables.set('mcpSession', session); }",
          "  const text = pm.response.text();",
          "  if (text) {",
          "    const sent = JSON.parse(pm.variables.replaceIn(pm.request.body.raw));",
          "    const frames = (pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type') || '').includes('text/event-stream')",
          "      ? text.split(/\\r?\\n\\r?\\n/).map(f => f.split(/\\r?\\n/).filter(l => l.startsWith('data:')).map(l => l.slice(5).trim()).join('\\n')).filter(Boolean).map(f => JSON.parse(f))",
          "      : [JSON.parse(text)];",
          "    const reply = frames.find(f => f.id === sent.id) || frames[0];",
          "    pm.variables.set('rpc', JSON.stringify(reply));",
          "  }",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
